          ],
          "content": "1. Anagh mixes 600 mL of orange juice with 900 mL of apple juice to make a fruit drink. Write the ratio of orange juice to apple juice in its simplest form."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.634,
            0.849,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": "2. Last year, we hired 3 buses for the school trip. We had a total of 162 students and teachers who went on that trip and all the buses were full. This year we have 204 students. How many buses will we need? Will all the buses be full?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.714,
            0.723,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": "3. The area of Delhi is 1,484 sq. km and the area of Mumbai is 550 sq. km. The population of Delhi is approximately 30 million and that of Mumbai is 20 million people. Which city is more crowded? Why do you say so?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.793,
            0.724,
            0.869
          ],
          "content": "4. A crane of height 155 cm has its neck and the rest of its body in the ratio 4 : 6. For your height, if your neck and the rest of the body also had this ratio, how tall would your neck be?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.872,
            0.724,
            0.933
          ],
          "content": "5. Let us try an ancient problem from Lilavati. At that time weights were measured in a unit named palas and niskas was a unit of money. “If 2 1palas of saffron"
